{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-201795-r4509168","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Apple Stuffing","sourcePageId":201795,"sourceRevision":"4509168","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-14T19:56:22Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Apple%20Stuffing&oldid=4509168","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:53.744Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using apple","Category:Recipes using cream of tartar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using fruit preserves","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"11fd0513fa892326c5eea1123f6cc1e5fe4494ed8d63659a8f6d04fb372f97e2","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Apple recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis works great as a stuffing for [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] chops and pork roasts. It also works well as a side with [[Cookbook:Roasting|roast]] [[Cookbook:Turkey|turkey]].\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Cornbread (disambiguation)|cornbread]], crumbled finely\n* ½ cup dried [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]]\n* ½ cup apple jelly\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Walnut|walnuts]], roughly [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[Cookbook:Kosher Salt|Kosher salt]]\n* Freshly ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Egg Yolk|egg yolks]], beaten\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Egg White|egg whites]], beaten to stiff peaks with ⅛ tsp [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]]\n* ¼ cup shredded [[Cookbook:Fontina|Fontina cheese]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine all ingredients except cheese and egg whites. Gently [[Cookbook:Folding|fold]] in whipped egg whites, in a few batches.\n#Pour into a roasting pan. Top with shredded cheese and [[Cookbook:Bake|bake]] at 325°F for 30 minutes, or until browned and bubbly on top.\n#Remove and let rest for 7 minutes. Serve warm or use for [[Cookbook:Apple Stuffed Pork Chops|Apple Stuffed Pork Chops]].\n\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fruit preserves]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Apple Stuffing","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ cups cornbread, crumbled finely","sourceText":"1½ cups cornbread, crumbled finely","amountText":"1½ cups cornbread, crumbled finely","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup dried apples","sourceText":"½ cup dried apples","amountText":"½ cup dried apples","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ cup apple jelly","sourceText":"½ cup apple jelly","amountText":"½ cup apple jelly","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"¼ cup walnuts, roughly chopped","sourceText":"¼ cup walnuts, roughly chopped","amountText":"¼ cup walnuts, roughly chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Kosher salt","source